rag system caution
chapter scoped query/filtering is only soft steered using prompt, underlying reason why hard filtering during query is quite impossible is because after ingestion, an entity can be pointed to by multiple documents

no reindex job (not available, deliberately deferred)
a workspace pins its embedding model at creation (workspaces.embedding_model_key)
and keeps it for life; nothing re-embeds an existing corpus into a different
model. cost is proportional to total corpus size rather than to what changed, so
it is the one operation whose price is unbounded by what the user just did.
consequences while it does not exist: retargeting the embedding default only
affects new workspaces, a model in use can never be deleted or lose its
provider, and every embedding_dim in use must always keep at least one enabled
model behind it (same dimension from another provider or self-hosted is fine).
if this is built: needs to be a job with progress + credit reservation, must
rewrite rag_chunk_vectors_<dim> and rag_contents.embedding_* and
workspaces.embedding_* in one transaction per content, and must block search or
serve stale results while running.
